# Build artefacts and generated data.
# None of these belong in version control: they are either reproducible from
# source, or they are outputs of a run whose inputs are recorded elsewhere.

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.pyd
*.dll
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.installed.cfg
pip-wheel-metadata/

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
.tox/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- Test and tool binaries ---
# Compiled from tests/test_c_engine.c; rebuild rather than commit.
tests/test_c_engine
tests/test_c_engine.exe

# --- Generated corpora ---
# Reproduced from the OSV bulk feed by the harvester; tens of megabytes.
_full_dataset*.json
_balanced*.json
_merged_*.json
_testing_*.json
testingMassiveDataset.json
_fresh_synthetic.json
_targeted_synthetic.json
_curated_blocks.json
_misclassified_blocks.json
# --- data/: bulk is ignored, measurements are published ---
#
# Two different kinds of file live here and they are treated differently on
# purpose. The corpora are bulk: multi-megabyte collections of third-party source
# that tools/build_corpus.py regenerates from the advisories, and which no reader
# benefits from having in the repository. The measurements are the opposite --
# a few kilobytes each, and the only way anyone can check a number quoted in
# docs/benchmark.md.
#
# Ignored, regenerated:
data/*.jsonl
data/adjudication_queue.json
data/cve_pairs.jsonl
data/corpus.jsonl
data/*.json

# Published, so every figure in the docs is checkable against its source:
!data/competitor_benchmark.json
!data/risk_benchmark.json
!data/corpus_manifest.json

# Deliberately NOT published: data/benchmark.json. It reports precision, recall,
# f1, false_positive_rate and abstention_rate, which are the measurements of the
# retired classifier and are withdrawn along with the rest of that section in
# docs/benchmark.md. It is also stale -- it predates the guard-as-evidence change
# -- so publishing it would put numbers in the repository that contradict the
# documentation. docs/risk-model.md defines what this project reports; that file
# does not.

# --- Model bundles and exported engines ---
*.joblib
syrth_model.joblib
syrth_ensemble*.joblib
syrth_meta*.joblib
syrth_engine.h
syrth_engine.so
models/

# --- paper/ ---
# The paper is the withdrawn artefact, so it is not tracked: main.tex,
# references.bib and the 367 KB main.pdf describe the methodology whose figures
# paper/WITHDRAWN.md withdraws. Keeping it would put the claim and its retraction
# side by side with nothing to say which one holds.
#
# paper/WITHDRAWN.md IS tracked, and it is deliberately not covered by the pattern
# below. It is not the paper; it is the claim-by-claim audit of what the paper got
# wrong, and roughly twenty-five documents link to it. WITHDRAWN.md alone would be
# a retraction with no claim attached, which withdraws nothing.
paper/*
!paper/WITHDRAWN.md

# --- v1 corpora ---
# The retired pipeline's datasets were versioned here once, at about 44 MB, and
# are regenerated rather than tracked: they are inputs to a model whose numbers
# are withdrawn, and paper/WITHDRAWN.md documents why by describing defects in code
# rather than by pointing at a blob. legacy/v1-artifacts/README.md records this.
_balanced_dataset*.json
_full_dataset*.json
_merged_*.json
_testing_*.json
testingMassiveDataset.json

# --- Learned-model weights ---
# syrth_codebert/ is 479 MB (a CodeBERT encoder: model.safetensors plus its
# tokenizer). It is an installable artefact, not source, and the only copy in this
# tree is the local one -- anyone using it needs to fetch it deliberately rather
# than inherit it from the clone. Recorded here so the absence is a decision
# rather than an oversight.
syrth_codebert/
*.safetensors

# Note: RLTESTS/ is *tracked*, not ignored. Those are the smoke-test fixtures --
# deliberately vulnerable sample modules used to check that the scanner still
# fires. They are source for the test suite, so they belong in the repository even
# though every file in them is insecure on purpose.

# --- Scratch space used by the external patch backend ---
.syrth-patch/

# --- Local scratch work ---
# One-off analysis scripts and the outputs of the retired v1 pipeline. Kept on
# disk for the audit trail in legacy/README.md, never committed: those outputs
# visualise figures that paper/WITHDRAWN.md withdraws.
experiments/scratch/

# --- Editor / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Logs ---
__run.log
__install.log
*.log
